 		<p>An Archetype does not dictate personality. On an uncertain task, it changes what is possible or at stake, not the throw. A character without the relevant Archetype may need instruction, equipment, information, or another approach. The descriptions are not exhaustive.</p>
 		<p><em>Examples: A Burglar can open a difficult lock but may throw to finish before a patrol arrives. A Sage can interpret a damaged manuscript but may throw to determine how much survives.</em></p>
-		<p>Archetypes that do not fit the setting, or whose names would be better if changed, may be done so. But next to the altered name, in parantheses add the functional Archetype.</p>
