+		<h4 id="narrative-archetypes">Narrative Archetypes</h4>
+		<h5 id="alchemist">Alchemist</h5>
+		<p>You understand reagents, furnaces, distillation, metallurgy, mineral salts, acids, poisons, and the signs of alchemical work. With a suitable laboratory, you can assay common substances, preserve reagents, and follow a known formula without a throw unless that formula says otherwise.</p>
+		<p>You may analyze unknown compounds, improvise substitutes, refine rare materials, or reconstruct incomplete formulae. This Archetype does not bypass the requirements for poisons, apothecary preparations, or alchemical potions. At the Referee's discretion, you may know apothecaries, miners, glassmakers, physicians, poisoners, or patrons seeking impossible transformations.</p>
+		<h5 id="bard">Bard</h5>
+		<p>You understand songs, stories, instruments, verse, performance, oral history, reputation, and the temper of an audience. You can entertain an ordinary crowd, recall well-known tales and lineages, and recognize familiar performers or traditions without a throw.</p>
+		<p>You may hold an audience’s attention while it is willing to listen, improvise a performance for a particular purpose, preserve information in verse, or trace news through songs and gossip. Performance cannot compel attention or control an audience. This Archetype grants no magical music. At the Referee's discretion, you may know innkeepers, courtiers, heralds, actors, poets, patrons, travelers, or rival performers.</p>
+		<h5 id="beast-master">Beast Master</h5>
 		<p>You understand animal behavior, feeding, breeding, injury, and distress. With time and materials, you can care for, restrain, and train domesticated animals without a throw.</p>
 		<p>You may calm, train, or convey simple intentions to wild or dangerous animals when their nature permits. At the Referee's discretion, you may know handlers, herders, hunters, stablekeepers, or remote communities.</p>
