+		<p>Choose an overland or overseas trade and whether it was legal or illicit. An overland Merchant understands pack animals, wagons, cargo, camps, tolls, and caravan discipline. An overseas Merchant understands ports, manifests, freight, customs, shipowners, and maritime trade routes, but cannot navigate or handle a vessel as a Mariner. A legal Merchant emphasizes contracts, guilds, and officials. An illicit Merchant emphasizes contraband, covert transfers, concealed cargo, and compromised officials, but does not gain the Intriguer’s expertise with forgery, false identities, or criminal politics.</p>
